{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.Introduction.main_theorem_statement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.Introduction.main_theorem_statement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.Introduction.main_theorem_statement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.Introduction.main_theorem_statement","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/Introduction/main_theorem_statement.lean#L59-L93","doc":"**Freeness theorem — canonical-form core.**\n\nFor a Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys` (admissible order `ord`), every\nalgebra element `f` admits a normal form, and *any two* normal\nforms of `f` coincide. The normal forms are precisely the elements\nof the remainder module `Õ(G)` (those whose support avoids every\nleading monomial of `sys`), so this is the statement that the\ncanonical-form map `A → Õ(G)` descends to a well-defined injection\n`A/I ↪ Õ(G)` — the substantive content the former `holds : Prop`\nlacked.\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete conjunction over `AlgElement`** (an\nexistential `ReducesToNF` plus a `∀`-uniqueness clause), not a bare\n`Prop` field. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:ugb-main","label":"thm:ugb-main","md":"unital-groebner-bases/introduction/ugb-main-theorem-statement.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}